Within the $U_1$ leptoquark model, we investigate the decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, taking into account both theoretical and experimental uncertainties to derive constraints on the model's parameters from $B$-meson decay data. Key processes considered are $B^- 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, $B^0 	o p  ar{	au}  ar{
u}$, $B^0 	o K^+ 	au  ar{
u}$, and $B^0 	o K^+  ar{\ell}  ar{
u}$, with $B^0 	o K^+ 	au  ar{
u}$ providing the primary constraints on the leptoquark's parameters due to the absence of $B^0 	o K^+ 	au  ar{
u}$ data. Using these derived $U_1$ leptoquark parameters, we then assess the feasibility of the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay.
